    "explanation": "To the rider: your SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is refunded in full. To the driver: the fee is not chargeable because the waiting period you are required to hold was not completed, and no compensation is payable out of it. The parties agree, and the record confirms, that you did reach the pickup: EV-TRIP-00203 records an 'arrived' event at 19:41:35 and EV-GPS-00203 holds 21 qualifying fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, so POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) and the POL-NS-02 proximity test are satisfied. The case is decided on POL-NS-01 limb (c), which measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix (19:41:20) and not from the arrival tap. On that measure the driver's own trace shows a single continuous in-geofence run of 195 seconds — 105 seconds short of the 300-second STANDARD minimum — and EV-TRIP-00203 corroborates the shortfall (arrived_at 19:41:35 to cancelled_at 19:44:40 is 185 seconds; wait_time_min 3.1). The driver's claim that limb (d) is independently made out by the RIDER_NO_SHOW code and the absence of a boarding event is rejected: limb (d) also requires termination at or after the moment the required dwell elapsed, and the trip was cancelled before it did. The accumulation route in POL-NS-06(i) is unavailable: the trace shows one in-geofence interval only (run_count 1, longest_run_sec 195.0), and the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00203-01 is MISSING with a null payload (weight 0.0), so its absence is citable but nothing may be added to the 195 seconds. POL-NS-06 therefore applies: the cancellation fee 'is not chargeable and is refunded to the rider in full', and the amount is SGD 4.00 — the cancellation_fee line and the whole of total_charged on EV-FARE-00203, where payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-07 compensates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and POL-NS-06 states that where the cumulative dwell still falls short the full refund stands and no driver compensation is payable, so the SGD 3.20 shown in the fare breakdown's derived block is not funded from this fee. POL-NS-04 does not apply — the driver's 19:44:31 reply came 101 seconds after the rider's 19:42:50 message, inside the 120-second window — and POL-NS-05 does not fire, since at the arrival marker the driver was stationary well within 300 m of the pin, so no false-arrival referral arises. No escalation ground is engaged: there is no clock skew, trace gap, chat defect or fare mismatch under POL-NS-08 (cancellation_fee 4.00 equals the GREATER of the STANDARD zone fee and the RYDE_X tier fee, both 4.00); the POL-NS-07 anti-farming pair is not met (2 no-show terminations against 131 completed trips in 30 days); and neither counterparty-dispute count reaches POL-NS-09(c). The profile fields were used only as context and for the checks that name them."
